fonts/: commit the proofing set, each font with its license alongside

Three fonts that were sitting untracked in `fonts/`, each committed together with the license
text that came with it. `fonts/` is the proofing space — this is deliberately not `docs/fonts/`,
which is the real set.

| font | license alongside |
|---|---|
| `BLKCHCRY.TTF` | `BLACKCHA.readme.txt` — Black Chancery, 1991, autotraced from a public-domain bitmap font |
| `Beyond Wonderland.ttf` | `Beyond Wonderland.readme.txt` — free for commercial use, donation to a koala hospital suggested |
| `GroutpixFlow-Regular.ttf` | **none present** |

## Why the license files come too

The seven fonts already tracked in `fonts/` have no license text with them. That is the thing
worth changing here, not the file count: a proofing space accumulates typefaces from many places,
and the terms are only reconstructable while you still remember where each one came from. Kept
next to the font, they survive the forgetting.

`GroutpixFlow-Regular.ttf` has no accompanying license file. Committed anyway, because a proofing
space is exactly where that is tolerable — but it is the one that would need its terms sourced
before it could graduate to `docs/fonts/`.

## What is deliberately not here

**Adine Kirnberg** — it did not make the cut, so it is not in this commit. Worth recording why it
would have needed a decision regardless: its license is the 1001Fonts FFC, which is free for
commercial use but says the font *"may not be sold or published without written permission"* and
is meant to travel as its original zip. This repository is public. Whether committing counts as
publishing is a real question, and it is now moot.

The two Kirnberg files are still untracked on disk — removing them is a `rm`, not a revert, so
they were left alone.

